From e9f67ec2aac3a55152c9a85e697c01fbc19be24c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:31:08 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] kcm_app-permissions: Flatpak refs read in a thread, app list
 and gamemode lookup after the first frame
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Device (list of apps, each app a sub-page via ConfigModule.push; docs/page-design.md §1, already so in master:
sidebar list with search, Permissions.qml per app, FlatpakPermissions.qml below it). No label, setting or permission
changed. NOT BUILT YET (owner stopped heavy work); checked statically only.

Changed:
- "Manage Flatpak Settings" (per-app toolbar action) now waits for kcm.referencesLoaded.
- Busy indicator in the app list after 150 ms while the list is read (kcm.appsModel.loading).
- Relabel table inventory/relabel/kcm_app-permissions.tsv (outer repo; labels unchanged). 25 inventory rows kept (ksr
  markers at the end of the QML/cpp files that hold them): inventory_check --kcm kcm_app-permissions --strict: 0 lost.

Speed (cause found in code):
- kcm.cpp constructor initialised m_references with FlatpakReference::allFlatpakReferences(): libflatpak lists the
  installed refs of every system installation plus the user one and reads appdata of each (flatpakreference.cpp:133-177),
  synchronously before the page. Now a QThread runs it (the references are moved to the GUI thread; destructor waits);
  the "open app X" argument (args / activationRequested) is kept in m_pendingArgs and opened once both the main UI and the
  references are ready (openPendingReference).
- AppsModel::loadApps() (KApplicationTrader::query, may rebuild KSycoca) ran in the constructor: now QTimer::singleShot(0)
  (ensureLoaded(), called early by openPendingReference if needed).
- gamemodeAvailable() did a blocking activatableServiceNames().value() on first use: now an async ListActivatableNames
  call, NOTIFY property.
- The 11 PermissionStore tables were already read with async D-Bus calls (left as is).
After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Not built yet; uncertain: QDBusConnectionInterface::asyncCall("ListActivatableNames") shape; libflatpak calls from a
worker thread (separate installation objects, no shared state with the GUI thread); FlatpakReference objects created in
the thread then moveToThread; ~AppPermissionsKCM is new in the header.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
